# UI label casing (English)

Use **Title Case** for user-facing labels and headings:

- Page/modal titles: `Create Client`, `Edit Vendor`, `Client Details`
- Section headings: `Organization Information`, `Address Information`
- Field labels: `Client Name`, `Address Line 1`, `Postal / ZIP Code`
- Table column headers: `Issue Date`, `Last Updated`
- Detail metadata rows: `Created At`, `Modified By`

## Rules

- Capitalize **every word** in labels/headings (not sentence case).
- Preserve acronyms: `ZIP`, `QR`, `ID`, `URL`, `PIN`, `PO`, `HR`, `VAT`, `API`.
- Keep **subtitles**, hints, placeholders, error messages, and long descriptions in **sentence case**.
- Prefer `messages/en.json` (`next-intl`) over hardcoded strings in components.
- Spanish (`messages/es.json`) follows normal Spanish capitalization, not English Title Case.

## Examples

| Avoid | Prefer |
|-------|--------|
| Create client | Create Client |
| Client name | Client Name |
| Address line 1 | Address Line 1 |
| Last updated | Last Updated |
| New pin status | New PIN Status |

Run `node scripts/apply-title-case.mjs` after bulk i18n updates.
